<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-9821] IgnitePdsCacheConfigurationFileConsistencyCheckTest is flaky in master</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-9821</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The test fails with timeout, a node is waiting for activation to complete.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Example of the fail:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/viewLog.html?buildId=2035822&amp;amp;buildTypeId=IgniteTests24Java8_PdsDirectIo1&amp;amp;tab=buildResultsDiv&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/viewLog.html?buildId=2035822&amp;amp;buildTypeId=IgniteTests24Java8_PdsDirectIo1&amp;amp;tab=buildResultsDiv&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Root cause of the hang is subject to investigate.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;From the build log I see that a node fails to process node start request because it fails to register one of the MBeans. Unrolling the logs earlier, I see that there is a failure from &lt;tt&gt;rebuildIndexesFromHash&lt;/tt&gt; which throws an exception because node is stopping. &lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
